From: pgandroid project <pgandroid@progalaxy.io>
Date: 2026-02-22
Subject: [PATCH 001] Android platform detection, headers, and __ANDROID_PGANDROID__ guards

This patch creates the Android platform port infrastructure:

1. src/include/port/android.h
   - New port header for Android (mirrors emscripten.h / wasi.h)
   - Defines I_ANDROID_PGANDROID guard
   - Includes android_pgandroid.h (the Android equivalent of wasm_common.h)

2. src/include/port/android_pgandroid.h
   - Android equivalent of wasm_common.h
   - Defines ANDROID_USERNAME, ANDROID_PGOPTS
   - Provides proc_exit → pg_proc_exit rename
   - Provides malloc-based SysV shared memory stubs (when PG_SHMEM defined)
   - Provides locale file stub for OpenPipeStream (when PG_FD defined)
   - Routes PostgreSQL logging to Android logcat
   - JNI I/O buffer declarations

3. src/template/android
   - Autoconf template for Android NDK builds
   - Sets UNNAMED_POSIX semaphores, -D_GNU_SOURCE, fPIC flags

4. Guard additions: __ANDROID_PGANDROID__ alongside existing WASM guards
   All existing #if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__wasi__) guards
   in the GENERIC_SINGLE_PROCESS category now also activate on Android.

